# Files copied into each new Claude Code worktree.
#
# A worktree is a fresh checkout, so it starts with everything git tracks and
# nothing git ignores. Gitignore syntax; only ignored paths are candidates,
# and they are copied (symlinks are skipped), so keep this list to what the
# project genuinely cannot run without.

# Secrets and local configuration. Without this the dev server boots but every
# route that talks to Supabase, Mailgun or Studio fails, and `.env.example` is
# tracked so it is no substitute.
.env

# 786MB, and copied per worktree - but the alternative is `npm ci` in every one,
# which needs the network and rebuilds sharp and better-sqlite3 natively. If
# disk becomes the problem, drop this line and install per worktree instead.
node_modules/

# Deliberately not copied:
#
#   .nuxt/       regenerated by dev/build/typecheck, and a copy from another
#                branch is stale state that misreports itself
#   .data/       the dev content database; a stale copy serves the wrong content
#   .output/     a build of a different branch
#   .claude/     never copy this - worktrees live under `.claude/worktrees/`,
#                so copying it would nest a checkout inside every checkout.
#                Claude Code also refuses to copy `settings.local.json`
#   .idea/       IDE state, per checkout
#   *.tsbuildinfo  a cache keyed to the tree it was built from
